      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Apply It: Approach Conversion and Documentation",
        content: `**On-the-job principle**: PCS Guideline **B5.2** states — "Procedures performed using the **open approach with percutaneous endoscopic assistance** are coded to the open approach." That is, **the final method that reached the site wins**.

**Common scenario — conversion**: A surgeon starts a **laparoscopic cholecystectomy** (Percutaneous Endoscopic, **4**). During the procedure, bleeding requires conversion to an **open** procedure. **Final code**: use **approach 0 (Open)** — NOT 4. PCS does not separately code the abandoned attempt; documentation should note "conversion to open."

**Another trap — robotic surgery**: Robotic (da Vinci) procedures use port-based access plus camera. **Approach: Percutaneous Endoscopic (4)** — same as standard laparoscopy. The robot is just a tool, not a separate approach.

**Documentation requirements**: For accurate approach selection, the op report must specify:
- Where the surgeon entered the body
- Whether a scope or camera was used
- Whether any conversion occurred

**CCA exam tactic**: when in doubt, identify the **final method** that reached the procedure site. Read carefully for words like "conversion," "via," "through," and "scope" — they are approach signals.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="34" font-weight="bold">Approach in the Real World</text><text x="550" y="105" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Conversion, robotic, and documentation</text><g><rect x="60" y="140" width="980" height="240" fill="#16213e" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="4" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="180" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">CONVERSION SCENARIO</text><line x1="80" y1="200" x2="1020" y2="200" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"/><text x="80" y="245" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Start:</text><text x="200" y="245" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Lap chole (Approach 4)</text><text x="80" y="285" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Event:</text><text x="200" y="285" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Bleeding - converted to open</text><text x="80" y="325" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Final approach:</text><text x="320" y="325" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">0 (Open)</text><text x="80" y="365" fill="#888" font-size="18">PCS Guideline B5.2 - final method wins</text></g><g><rect x="60" y="410" width="980" height="200" fill="#16213e" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="4" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="450" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b5cf6" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">ROBOTIC SURGERY</text><line x1="80" y1="470" x2="1020" y2="470" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="2"/><text x="80" y="515" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Tool:</text><text x="200" y="515" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">da Vinci robot via trocar ports</text><text x="80" y="555" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Approach:</text><text x="250" y="555" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">4 (Percutaneous Endoscopic)</text><text x="80" y="595" fill="#888" font-size="18">Robot = tool not separate approach</text></g><g><rect x="60" y="640" width="980" height="200" fill="#16213e" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="4" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="680" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">DOC REQUIREMENTS</text><line x1="80" y1="700" x2="1020" y2="700" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="740" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20">Entry point - skin? natural opening?</text><text x="100" y="775" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20">Scope used? - yes/no</text><text x="100" y="810" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20">Conversion? - document it</text></g><g><rect x="60" y="870" width="980" height="180" fill="#16213e" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="3" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="910" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">CCA Word Triggers</text><text x="100" y="950" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">"laparoscopic":</text><text x="370" y="950" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">approach 4</text><text x="100" y="985" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">"via mouth/anus":</text><text x="370" y="985" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">approach 7 or 8</text><text x="100" y="1020" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">"skin lesion":</text><text x="370" y="1020" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">approach X</text></g></svg>`,
          caption: "Final method wins. Robotic = approach 4. Always check for conversion language."
        }
      }
