        type: "concept",
        title: "MDM and Time — The Two Paths",
        content: `**Medical Decision Making (MDM)** is scored on **three elements**; the **final level = the middle of the three** (or two of three at the same level):

- **Problems addressed** — minimal, low, moderate, high (e.g., 1 stable chronic = low; 1 chronic with exacerbation = moderate; 1 chronic with severe exacerbation = high)
- **Data reviewed/ordered** — labs, imaging, independent historian, independent interpretation
- **Risk of complications** — minimal OTC management → low (Rx mgmt) → moderate (prescription drug mgmt) → high (drug therapy requiring intensive monitoring, decision re: hospitalization)

**Time thresholds (NEW patient):** **99202** = 15–29 min; **99203** = 30–44 min; **99204** = 45–59 min; **99205** = 60–74 min.

**Time thresholds (ESTABLISHED patient):** **99212** = 10–19 min; **99213** = 20–29 min; **99214** = 30–39 min; **99215** = 40–54 min.

Time includes **non-face-to-face work the same day** — chart prep, ordering, documenting, care coordination.`,
