      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Real-World: The OIG's Favorite Audit Target",
        content: `**Modifier -25** is the #1 modifier-related audit target. The **OIG** (Office of Inspector General) repeatedly publishes reports finding that **30-50% of -25 claims fail documentation review**. Common findings: providers routinely append -25 to every E/M billed with a procedure, even when the E/M is just the **pre-procedure exam** (not separately identifiable).

**Compliance rules HIM coders must enforce:**
- The E/M note must **stand alone** — could the physician have billed the E/M if the procedure hadn't happened?
- **Document the separate problem** addressed by the E/M (different chief complaint, different diagnosis)
- Pre-procedure assessment **bundled into the procedure** does NOT qualify
- Link distinct ICD-10 diagnoses to E/M and procedure when possible

**Modifier -59 abuse** is similar — used to bypass NCCI edits without justification. Medicare's **-X{EPSU}** subset was created specifically to **force coders to be more specific**, reducing -59 misuse. Always pick the most granular modifier; use -59 only when nothing else fits.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="36" font-weight="bold">OIG -25 Audit Survival Checklist</text><g><rect x="60" y="100" width="980" height="240" rx="14" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.25" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="3"/><text x="100" y="140" fill="#ef4444" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Why -25 Gets Audited</text><text x="100" y="180" fill="#ffffff" font-size="19">- OIG: 30-50% of -25 claims fail documentation review</text><text x="100" y="215" fill="#ffffff" font-size="19">- Providers attach -25 automatically to every E/M+procedure pair</text><text x="100" y="250" fill="#ffffff" font-size="19">- Pre-procedure exam is NOT separately billable</text><text x="100" y="285" fill="#ffffff" font-size="19">- Repayment demands can exceed millions of dollars</text><text x="100" y="320" fill="#ffd700" font-size="19">- HIM compliance audit programs must screen -25 use</text></g><text x="550" y="395" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="32" font-weight="bold">The Stand-Alone Test</text><g><rect x="60" y="420" width="980" height="80" rx="12" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.3" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="470" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">1.</text><text x="160" y="470" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Could the E/M be billed if no procedure happened?</text></g><g><rect x="60" y="515" width="980" height="80" rx="12" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.3" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="565" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">2.</text><text x="160" y="565" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Is there a separate chief complaint or diagnosis?</text></g><g><rect x="60" y="610" width="980" height="80" rx="12" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.3" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="660" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">3.</text><text x="160" y="660" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Does the E/M note document work beyond pre-procedure?</text></g><g><rect x="60" y="705" width="980" height="80" rx="12" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.3" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="755" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">4.</text><text x="160" y="755" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Can you link a different ICD-10 to the E/M vs procedure?</text></g><text x="550" y="830" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="28" font-weight="bold">All YES = -25 supported. Any NO = drop modifier!</text><g><rect x="60" y="870" width="980" height="160" rx="14" fill="#8b5cf6" opacity="0.25" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="915" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b5cf6" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">-59 Compliance Rule</text><text x="550" y="955" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Always pick the most specific modifier first</text><text x="550" y="990" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">-LT, -RT, -XE, -XS, -XP, -XU BEFORE -59</text><text x="550" y="1020" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="18">Medicare flags routine -59 use as audit-worthy</text></g></svg>`,
          caption: "Run every -25 through the stand-alone test before submitting the claim."
        }
      }
