        explanation: "ICD-10-CM codes are updated annually effective October 1, the start of the federal fiscal year. CMS publishes the addenda in summer (typically August in the IPPS Final Rule) so coders, encoders, and payers have time to prepare, but the codes do not take effect until October 1. Using new codes before October 1 will cause denials because the codes are not yet active in payer systems. Using deleted codes after October 1 will also cause denials. CPT (January 1) and ICD-10-CM (October 1) have different cycles. Encoder push dates are coordinated with the effective date, not a substitute for it.",
