        content: `Your fingerprints touch every part of this stack. **CDS**: when a coding query is needed because a CDS alert prompted a documentation change, document the alert reference in your query trail. **E-prescribing**: when reconciling med lists for coding, verify the **EPCS prescription audit trail** for controlled-substance encounters. **Lab/Radiology**: if an interface drops, results may post to charts hours late — flag any encounter coded without results that should have been available. **Patient portal**: respond to patient requests for amendments under HIPAA — never block, route formally. **MPI**: report suspected duplicates and overlays to the **HIM data integrity team immediately** — don't code under a chart you suspect is contaminated. Your CCA credential expects you to **recognize the seams** between systems and to **escalate** when data integrity is at risk.`,
