        explanation: "**TEFCA** (Trusted Exchange Framework and Common Agreement) authorizes exchange for **treatment** without requiring a new patient authorization — the **C-CDA** flows through a **QHIN** (Qualified Health Information Network) after the request is verified. HIPAA's TPO (Treatment, Payment, Operations) clause already permits this; TEFCA is the **technical and trust layer** that makes it interoperable. Paper mail and re-authorization would defeat the entire purpose of national health information exchange.",
