        options: [
          { text: "Payment is based on patient characteristics, with the primary ICD-10-CM diagnosis driving the PT, OT, and SLP clinical categories", correct: true },
          { text: "Payment is based on total therapy minutes delivered per week, the same as RUG-IV", correct: false },
          { text: "Payment is a flat per-diem rate that does not vary by patient acuity or diagnosis", correct: false },
          { text: "Payment is based on the patient's age and length of stay only, with diagnosis ignored", correct: false }
        ],
        explanation: `**Correct: patient characteristics driven by ICD-10-CM coding.** PDPM (effective October 1, 2019) replaced the RUG-IV system precisely to eliminate the perverse incentive of therapy-minute-driven payment. Under PDPM, the **primary diagnosis** maps to a **clinical category** (e.g., Major Joint Replacement, Cardiovascular, Pulmonary) that drives PT, OT, and SLP classification. **Comorbidities** drive NTA scoring and SLP add-ons. The per-diem still has variable adjustments over time (PT/OT decline after day 20; NTA after day 3), but the foundation is patient acuity expressed through accurate, specific diagnosis coding.`,
