        explanation: "This is classic **unbundling** — billing component codes when a **comprehensive bundled code (80048)** already includes them. **NCCI Procedure-to-Procedure (PTP) edits** catch this pattern. The standard fix is to bill the bundled code only; in rare cases where the components were truly separate (e.g., performed at different times for different clinical indications), modifier **-59** or **-X{EPSU}** may be applied with documentation. MUE governs unit limits, -50 is bilateral, and medical necessity is about diagnosis support — none apply here.",
